<title>USA: Washington Mutual seen as unlikely knight.</title>
<headline>Washington Mutual seen as unlikely knight.</headline>
<byline>Cal Mankowksi</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Washington Mutual Savings Bank would face tremendous obstacles if it jumped into the H.F. Ahmanson and Co -Great Western Financial Corp takeover battle as a white knight for Great Western, a Wall Street source familiar with the situation and close to Ahmanson said Monday.</p>
<p>For starters, the source said, Washington Mutual would be &quot;unable to get anywhere near the cost savings which the Ahmanson bid can generate.&quot; Ahmanson has said it could achieve annual cost savings of $400 million.</p>
</text>
